# The Wi-Fi keepalive drop test (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.wifidrop), on the jb system image so Sileo can
# be opened first: an application in front with idleTimerDisabled is what keeps SpringBoard from
# locking the display, and a locked display suspends this job (logs/095245-run.log,
# logs/100719-run.log). Then: join, an address and a name, net_test leave, and the keepalive
# should read the kernel link-off event, wait five seconds to tell a real loss from a join's own
# bounce, and join /redwood/fw/network again. The last lines are the proof.
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 300 &
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen sileo://package/wget
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 25
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 60 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 wait 5 tap 0.5 0.5 &
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 30 joinfile /redwood/fw/network
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60 resolve apt.procurs.us
/redwood/bin/net_test leave
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 10
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60
/redwood/bin/net_test resolve apt.procurs.us
